From b5c80e2578eb35ac98508ab10eb0ca28d52693f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:44:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mips: Emit the MIPS16 $gp setup at the function start
 [PR125582]

mips16_gp_pseudo_reg emits the $gp load in the topmost sequence before
its first real insn.  The scan skips CODE_LABELs, so the load can land
in a later block, and since r16-1398 that block can be expanded but not
BB_RTL yet, where add_insn_after crashes on BB_END.

Emit the load and the clobbers after entry_of_function () instead, as
other ports do.  Before construct_init_block that is not usable, but
everything after the first insn of the topmost sequence then becomes
the init block, so emit after that insn.  The current sequence does not
work there: expand_phi_nodes can call this while emitting the copies
for one PHI edge.  The entry edge does not work either: pass_expand
puts those insns after the parameter setup, which can itself use $gp.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5

	PR target/125582

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/mips/mips.cc (mips16_gp_pseudo_reg): Emit the $gp load
	and the clobbers after entry_of_function (), or after the first
	insn before the init block exists.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.target/mips/pr125582.c: New test.

Suggested-by: Jakub Jelinek <jakub@redhat.com>
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Link: https://inbox.sourceware.org/gcc-patches/20261017115008.132337-1-julius@bairaktaris.de/
---
 gcc/config/mips/mips.cc | 19 ++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

--- a/gcc/config/mips/mips.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/mips/mips.cc
@@ -3399,18 +3399,11 @@ mips16_gp_pseudo_reg (void)
 {
   if (cfun->machine->mips16_gp_pseudo_rtx == NULL_RTX)
     {
-      rtx_insn *scan;
-
       cfun->machine->mips16_gp_pseudo_rtx = gen_reg_rtx (Pmode);
 
-      push_topmost_sequence ();
-
-      scan = get_insns ();
-      while (NEXT_INSN (scan) && !INSN_P (NEXT_INSN (scan)))
-	scan = NEXT_INSN (scan);
-
+      start_sequence ();
       rtx set = gen_load_const_gp (cfun->machine->mips16_gp_pseudo_rtx);
-      rtx_insn *insn = emit_insn_after (set, scan);
+      rtx_insn *insn = emit_insn (set);
       INSN_LOCATION (insn) = 0;
       /* NewABI support hasn't been implement.  NewABI should generate RTL
 	 sequence instead of ASM sequence directly.  */
@@ -3419,6 +3412,14 @@ mips16_gp_pseudo_reg (void)
 	  emit_clobber (MIPS16_PIC_TEMP);
 	  emit_clobber (MIPS_PROLOGUE_TEMP (Pmode));
 	}
+      rtx_insn *seq = end_sequence ();
+
+      /* Until construct_init_block, everything after the first insn of
+	 the topmost sequence becomes the init block.  The current sequence
+	 can then be the copies on one PHI edge from expand_phi_nodes.  */
+      push_topmost_sequence ();
+      emit_insn_after (seq, (ENTRY_BLOCK_PTR_FOR_FN (cfun)->flags & BB_RTL
+			     ? entry_of_function () : get_insns ()));
       pop_topmost_sequence ();
     }
 
